WEBVTT

00:00.209 --> 00:04.796
I need to know the truth
about Hijikata Toshizo...

00:04.880 --> 00:09.092
He had the same look
in his eyes as you.

00:09.134 --> 00:11.678
What's the fun
in doing the sensible thing?

00:11.762 --> 00:17.476
Doing what no one else
can is what makes you a badass.

00:17.559 --> 00:19.686
[narrator] The time: the final
years of the Edo period.

00:21.647 --> 00:23.232
In a time of upheaval

00:23.273 --> 00:25.776
there were men who lived
fiercely and passionately

00:25.817 --> 00:26.944
by the way of the sword.

00:27.027 --> 00:29.905
To become...
the strongest man there is.

00:29.988 --> 00:33.158
What a coincidence. Same here.

00:34.493 --> 00:35.953
[chuckles]

00:36.036 --> 00:38.038
[Matsudaira]
I welcome you as the fools

00:38.121 --> 00:41.166
who are ready to die
alongside the Aizu!

00:42.626 --> 00:44.586
[narrator] Resisting
the relentless tide of history,

00:44.670 --> 00:46.046
they pressed on
with unwavering resolve.

00:46.129 --> 00:50.342
[♪♪♪]

00:50.425 --> 00:53.804
This is the story
of the last samurai

00:53.887 --> 00:56.306
men who bloomed brilliantly

00:56.348 --> 01:00.310
in an age of turmoil,
and then fell.

01:00.394 --> 01:02.521
Let us bloom with all our might.

01:07.025 --> 01:13.198
SONG OF THE SAMURAI

01:23.625 --> 01:25.669
APRIL 1862, TOSA

01:25.711 --> 01:27.670
[indistinct chatter]

01:27.713 --> 01:30.299
[seabirds calling]

01:34.761 --> 01:36.847
Man, Edo is amazing!

01:36.888 --> 01:38.265
[all exclaiming]

01:38.348 --> 01:40.017
It was packed with people,
and the food was delicious.

01:40.058 --> 01:44.354
And! And there were
a ton of strong fighters, too.

01:44.396 --> 01:48.942
But out of all of them, this guy
Toshi was the strongest.

01:49.026 --> 01:51.235
You just told us that story
about Toshi.

01:51.320 --> 01:53.155
That's the fifth time.

01:54.364 --> 01:56.908
Is that true, Ukichi?

01:56.991 --> 02:01.038
But still, Izo,
since it makes you laugh

02:01.121 --> 02:03.540
I'd be happy to hear it
five or six times!

02:03.624 --> 02:04.833
Hey!

02:04.916 --> 02:06.168
[all laughing]

02:06.251 --> 02:10.589
Never mind all that.
Did you get a taste of this?

02:12.257 --> 02:14.968
What? You eat pinky?

02:15.052 --> 02:17.054
You idiot! Edo has Yoshiwara,

02:17.095 --> 02:19.765
the land's greatest
pleasure district!

02:19.848 --> 02:24.186
I'm talking about women!

02:24.227 --> 02:29.066
[stammering]
I'm... not very good with women.

02:29.149 --> 02:32.194
I've never seen or "tasted"
anything like that.

02:32.277 --> 02:35.197
[all laughing]

02:37.240 --> 02:41.286
Hey, Izo! Master Takechi
is calling for you!

02:43.622 --> 02:45.082
[thunder rumbling]

02:45.123 --> 02:46.124
[Okada]
Assassination?

02:46.208 --> 02:47.709
[Oishi] Shh!

02:47.793 --> 02:49.628
Keep your voice down, Izo.

02:49.711 --> 02:52.297
[Okada]
But still, an assassination...

02:53.674 --> 02:56.218
[Takechi]
It's divine retribution, Izo.

02:57.135 --> 02:58.553
[Okada]
Divine retribution?

02:59.596 --> 03:01.682
We are to eliminate
Yoshida Toyo.

03:04.226 --> 03:05.477
Who's that?

03:06.561 --> 03:09.106
You don't even know who Toyo is?

03:09.147 --> 03:10.941
He's the ringleader in Tosa

03:10.982 --> 03:12.943
who oppresses
us lower-class samurai.

03:12.984 --> 03:15.779
He sides with the shogunate's
plan to open the country

03:15.862 --> 03:19.616
a vile man who is leading
our nation to ruin.

03:21.034 --> 03:22.786
Izo.

03:22.828 --> 03:26.540
You, too, are a member
of the Tosa Loyalist Party.

03:29.835 --> 03:32.254
Lend me your strength

03:32.337 --> 03:35.424
so we may restore the Emperor
and expel the foreigners.

03:42.139 --> 03:44.433
[thunder rumbling]

03:44.516 --> 03:47.352
Mmm...

03:48.353 --> 03:50.021
[inhales deeply]

03:51.565 --> 03:55.736
No, I can't do that.
Anything but that.

03:55.819 --> 03:57.154
Izo!

03:57.195 --> 04:00.157
Izo! You'd really turn down
Master Takechi?

04:00.198 --> 04:03.535
But...
I don't like killing people.

04:04.286 --> 04:05.579
I'm sorry.

04:07.497 --> 04:09.082
Hey! Get back here, Izo!
Wait, Izo!

04:09.166 --> 04:12.002
Let him go.
[Nasu] But, Master Takechi...

04:12.043 --> 04:14.421
Well, wait and see.

04:16.380 --> 04:18.550
[thunder rumbling]

04:21.803 --> 04:25.015
[man sobbing]

04:25.098 --> 04:26.767
[man]
Why would anyone do this?

04:30.061 --> 04:31.646
[sobbing]
Ukichi!

04:36.568 --> 04:37.736
Ukichi!

04:42.741 --> 04:44.201
Ukichi...

04:44.284 --> 04:45.994
Ukichi...

04:46.036 --> 04:48.580
[Nasu] They were making
an example of Ukichi's father!

04:50.040 --> 04:51.249
He petitioned the domain

04:51.332 --> 04:53.210
to lessen the burden
of the labor tax.

04:53.293 --> 04:55.420
[♪♪♪]

04:55.504 --> 04:57.422
And the one
who gave the order...

04:59.174 --> 05:00.592
it had to be Yoshida Toyo.

05:03.261 --> 05:04.554
That damn Toyo!

05:04.596 --> 05:07.724
How much more
will he make us suffer?

05:07.808 --> 05:10.769
[♪♪♪]

05:41.007 --> 05:42.467
Ukichi...

05:45.846 --> 05:46.972
Ukichi...

05:49.015 --> 05:50.642
[sniffles]

06:02.028 --> 06:03.071
I...

06:07.409 --> 06:08.994
will avenge...

06:12.956 --> 06:14.124
you.

06:19.379 --> 06:20.964
I'm sorry, Ukichi.

06:24.175 --> 06:25.594
I'm sorry, Izo.

06:46.364 --> 06:49.159
[Oishi] Yoshida Toyo!
It's divine retribution!

07:00.545 --> 07:03.048
You think a bunch
of Loyalist Party monkeys

07:04.883 --> 07:06.718
can take me down?

07:14.059 --> 07:15.060
[Okada]
Why?

07:17.687 --> 07:18.772
Why...

07:20.398 --> 07:22.567
Why did you kill Ukichi?

07:23.568 --> 07:25.779
Another one, huh?

07:27.322 --> 07:28.531
Ukichi...

07:30.784 --> 07:34.371
looked up to me
like an older brother.

07:34.454 --> 07:37.499
[Yoshida] What is this nonsense
you're spouting?

07:38.457 --> 07:40.877
You die first!

07:40.961 --> 07:41.962
[flesh rends]

07:43.338 --> 07:45.048
[thunder booms]

07:48.259 --> 07:50.887
Impossible...
that a lowly samurai...

07:53.473 --> 07:56.810
could be this skilled...

07:56.893 --> 08:00.438
[♪♪♪]

08:00.522 --> 08:02.399
[Oishi] Izo!

08:02.440 --> 08:03.900
[Nasu] You did it!

08:03.942 --> 08:07.362
It's divine retribution!
It's divine retribution!

08:07.445 --> 08:08.363
You did it, Izo!

08:08.446 --> 08:10.532
[Nasu & Oishi celebrating]

08:18.164 --> 08:20.792
And that was the beginning
of Izo the Manslayer.

08:22.585 --> 08:28.967
After that, following
Takechi Hanpeita's orders

08:29.050 --> 08:31.636
he cut down one key shogunate
official after another.

08:34.639 --> 08:38.476
So he was
a completely different man

08:38.559 --> 08:41.438
from when he met my grandfather,
Hijikata Toshizo.

08:41.520 --> 08:46.651
A different man?
That's putting it mildly.

08:46.735 --> 08:47.610
Eh?

08:47.694 --> 08:49.612
When a man with a kind soul

08:49.654 --> 08:52.407
is forced to keep killing
brutally...

08:52.490 --> 08:55.660
Do you know what happens to him?

09:01.541 --> 09:03.084
He shatters.

09:04.335 --> 09:05.879
Hold it!

09:05.962 --> 09:06.963
KYO, JULY 1863

09:07.839 --> 09:10.008
Surrender! Izo the Manslayer!

09:11.593 --> 09:12.844
Stay away.

09:15.013 --> 09:16.264
Don't come near.

09:16.347 --> 09:17.307
[all yell fiercely]

09:18.183 --> 09:22.062
[♪♪♪]

09:25.523 --> 09:29.736
[breathes deeply]

09:45.251 --> 09:48.213
[wind whistling]

10:06.564 --> 10:09.692
[baby crying]

10:23.706 --> 10:25.667
[man 1]
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

10:25.750 --> 10:27.585
Hey, what's going on?

10:27.669 --> 10:28.753
The Mibu Ronin are coming.

10:28.837 --> 10:30.547
The Mibu Roshigumi?

10:30.630 --> 10:34.592
[man 1]
Check out that cocky bastard
strutting at the very front.

10:34.676 --> 10:37.554
Rumor is
he killed Tanaka Shinbei.

10:37.637 --> 10:39.597
[man 2] Hijikata Toshizo,
the vice-commander?

10:39.681 --> 10:40.890
[man 3]
Yep.

10:40.974 --> 10:42.142
Toshizo?

10:45.770 --> 10:47.772
Hey, they're coming.
Yeah.

11:16.426 --> 11:19.345
[♪♪♪]

11:20.638 --> 11:23.183
[clattering]
[dog barking]

11:27.770 --> 11:29.314
What's up Toshi?

11:30.732 --> 11:33.234
I feel like we're being watched.

11:33.318 --> 11:34.777
Huh?

11:34.819 --> 11:36.321
A loyalist assassin?

11:38.781 --> 11:40.825
No, it's probably nothing.

12:06.476 --> 12:10.313
[narrator] By this time,
the Mibu Roshigumi had grown

12:10.355 --> 12:13.858
and was split
into two major factions.

12:15.193 --> 12:18.363
The first was led by
Commander Kondo Isami...

12:18.446 --> 12:19.697
[Hijikata] One!

12:19.781 --> 12:21.366
...with Vice-Commanders
Hijikata Toshizo

12:21.449 --> 12:24.494
and Yamanami Keisuke,

12:24.577 --> 12:27.747
the Shieikan faction.

12:27.830 --> 12:30.667
[Hijikata] One, two!
[all] One, two!

12:30.708 --> 12:35.088
One, two!
[all] One, two!

12:35.171 --> 12:37.674
[narrator] The other
was the Serizawa faction,

12:37.757 --> 12:40.343
led by First Commander
Serizawa Kamo

12:40.385 --> 12:43.179
Vice-Commander Niimi Nishiki

12:43.221 --> 12:49.435
and Assistant Vice-Commander
Hirayama Goro.

12:50.853 --> 12:53.648
[Todo] Don't tell me

12:53.731 --> 12:57.360
they went out drinking again
last night

12:57.443 --> 12:59.529
and still aren't back.

13:01.072 --> 13:04.784
[groaning]
Those bastards.

13:04.867 --> 13:06.744
Incredible!

13:06.828 --> 13:08.830
Mr. Todo
sure is impressive!

13:08.913 --> 13:10.999
How about that, Shimada?

13:13.126 --> 13:15.670
SHIMADA KAI

13:15.753 --> 13:17.714
Damn, Shimada!

13:17.755 --> 13:18.923
You're a beast!
Like a god of war!

13:19.007 --> 13:23.177
Hey, Shimada!
Don't get cocky, rookie.

13:23.261 --> 13:25.805
I'm sorry.
I got a little carried away.

13:25.888 --> 13:28.891
Put those down, now!
Put those down!

13:28.975 --> 13:31.894
All of you,
drop and give me push-ups!

13:32.937 --> 13:34.355
[Aridoshi]
Mr. Yamanami.

13:41.154 --> 13:47.368
[Todo] 11, 12, 13
[all] 11, 12, 13

13:47.452 --> 13:51.956
[Todo] 14, 15, 16...
[all] 14, 15, 16...

13:55.626 --> 13:57.128
[sighs]

14:00.423 --> 14:02.508
You want to switch
to the other faction?

14:05.470 --> 14:06.554
Tell me why.

14:07.930 --> 14:11.392
I wish to train
under Master Serizawa.

14:11.434 --> 14:15.813
They see more action,
and they're flush with cash.

14:15.897 --> 14:19.776
Plus, it's fun. They get
to party almost every night.

14:19.859 --> 14:21.402
[all] Exactly.

14:22.904 --> 14:24.322
So that's the real reason, huh?

14:25.114 --> 14:27.075
[students stammering]

14:27.116 --> 14:29.118
[laughing]

14:31.496 --> 14:32.997
Well, yeah.
That makes sense.

14:34.540 --> 14:36.084
[sighs]

14:36.167 --> 14:37.335
Fine.

14:38.586 --> 14:39.629
Do whatever you want.

14:39.670 --> 14:42.298
Huh? Are you serious?

14:42.382 --> 14:44.217
Yeah. But...

14:45.426 --> 14:47.178
on one condition.

14:48.971 --> 14:50.556
[Saito]
Wake up, Gen!

14:51.933 --> 14:53.518
It's starting again!

14:53.601 --> 14:57.063
[♪♪♪]

14:57.146 --> 14:58.272
Yes.

14:59.524 --> 15:03.861
Well, well, look who's all here.

15:03.945 --> 15:05.988
Hey. It hasn't started yet,
right?

15:06.030 --> 15:08.116
It starts now.

15:08.199 --> 15:09.826
Hey

15:09.909 --> 15:11.244
come at me at once.

15:12.995 --> 15:15.498
If you can land
just one strike on me

15:15.581 --> 15:18.501
you can go to Serizawa's group
or wherever the hell you want.

15:18.584 --> 15:19.669
Awesome.

15:19.710 --> 15:21.337
Not confident, even four-on-one?

15:21.421 --> 15:22.422
If you're that pathetic,

15:22.505 --> 15:24.173
they won't give you
the time of day.

15:26.843 --> 15:29.971
Hijikata,
mind if we add three more?

15:30.054 --> 15:31.931
Yeah. I don't care.

15:32.014 --> 15:33.182
That's seven men!

15:33.266 --> 15:35.351
But even for Mr. Hijikata,
that's...

15:35.393 --> 15:37.019
Oi.

15:39.147 --> 15:40.106
Hey.

15:41.190 --> 15:43.901
On guard!
C'mon, take it seriously!

15:43.985 --> 15:45.903
What are you, scared? Hey!

15:45.987 --> 15:47.613
There are seven of us!
We can win this!

15:47.697 --> 15:48.614
Yeah!

15:48.698 --> 15:50.408
Good luck.
Yeah.

15:50.491 --> 15:53.035
[students shouting]

15:53.119 --> 15:56.080
Get him! Get him!

16:03.546 --> 16:06.299
What's the matter? Bring it!

16:11.053 --> 16:13.055
[students coughs]

16:13.139 --> 16:14.098
Hey.

16:15.933 --> 16:17.268
So, I take it
you're all staying?

16:19.103 --> 16:22.398
Whoa! Look at you go, Toshi!

16:24.066 --> 16:28.696
That was pathetic, you guys.
Gen.

16:28.779 --> 16:30.281
Mm.

16:30.364 --> 16:31.324
What is this?

16:31.407 --> 16:33.159
Eh!

16:33.242 --> 16:34.076
Hey!

16:34.118 --> 16:35.495
I'll assist you.

16:37.997 --> 16:40.124
So it's against you two?

16:42.877 --> 16:45.379
Now this is getting interesting.

16:47.840 --> 16:51.260
[♪♪♪]

16:58.309 --> 17:00.019
[laughs]

17:14.325 --> 17:16.243
[exclaiming]

17:16.327 --> 17:17.118
Dammit!

17:17.203 --> 17:18.538
Hey, it's not a lethal blow.

17:18.621 --> 17:20.080
Awesome!

17:20.164 --> 17:22.415
Damn. He got me!

17:22.500 --> 17:25.086
[Nagakura]
Man, what were you thinking?

17:25.127 --> 17:28.339
What's the matter? You that
pissed off you lost to me?

17:28.422 --> 17:32.760
That's not it! You won the fight
against those guys, didn't you?

17:32.843 --> 17:34.971
Then why did you
run them all off?

17:35.054 --> 17:36.222
If they want to leave,

17:36.305 --> 17:37.723
there's no use
trying to stop them.

17:37.807 --> 17:39.100
[laughing]

17:39.183 --> 17:40.643
That's so like you, Toshi.

17:40.685 --> 17:43.312
There you go again,
being so nonchalant.

17:43.354 --> 17:47.149
Do you know how many men
we've lost to them this month?

17:47.233 --> 17:49.151
Pardon the intrusion.
Huh?

17:51.070 --> 17:54.365
You must all be tired.
Please, help yourselves.

17:54.448 --> 17:56.117
Perfect timing.

17:56.200 --> 17:58.494
You're always so thoughtful,
Aijiro.

17:58.578 --> 17:59.495
Not at all.

17:59.579 --> 18:00.496
SASAKI AIJIRO

18:00.580 --> 18:02.873
I'm honored you
remembered my name, sir.

18:02.957 --> 18:06.168
What are you so tense about?

18:06.210 --> 18:10.089
He's never this well-behaved
around me.

18:10.172 --> 18:13.634
Even in the last practice,
he mercilessly beat me down.

18:13.718 --> 18:15.011
That's not right.

18:15.052 --> 18:17.179
The one always beating me down
is you, Master!

18:17.263 --> 18:19.515
See? He's usually got
a much bigger mouth on him.

18:19.557 --> 18:22.852
What's this? Bragging about
your cute little disciple?

18:22.893 --> 18:24.312
[laughter]

18:27.565 --> 18:29.984
[sighing]

18:30.067 --> 18:31.193
But...

18:31.235 --> 18:33.154
is this really okay...

18:34.405 --> 18:37.283
for someone like me,
the son of a craftsman

18:37.366 --> 18:39.702
to join the Mibu Roshigumi?

18:42.204 --> 18:44.206
If you can't join our ranks,

18:44.248 --> 18:46.542
then we'd all have to quit
on the spot.

18:47.793 --> 18:48.878
Right, Toshi?

18:48.919 --> 18:50.379
Huh.

18:50.421 --> 18:52.923
We're just farm boys ourselves.

18:53.007 --> 18:54.216
[gasps]

18:54.300 --> 18:55.593
[Kondo]
Aijiro...

18:56.927 --> 18:58.804
being a samurai isn't about
your social status...

19:00.139 --> 19:01.557
It's about what's in here.

19:06.187 --> 19:08.939
Commander Kondo... Everyone...

19:09.023 --> 19:11.525
I swear, I absolutely swear...

19:11.609 --> 19:14.820
I will prove my worth
to all of you!

19:14.904 --> 19:17.281
Good. See that you do, Kojiro.

19:17.365 --> 19:19.492
It's Aijiro.
[Hijikata] Yeah, I know.

19:20.534 --> 19:21.911
Thank you.

19:21.994 --> 19:24.914
[slow clapping]

19:24.997 --> 19:28.167
[Saeki]
Man, that's something else..

19:30.211 --> 19:33.422
That master-disciple bond,
you know?

19:33.464 --> 19:37.259
It gets you right here.
Seriously, I'm so damn jealous.

19:37.301 --> 19:39.136
I want one of those too.

19:39.220 --> 19:40.763
What the hell do you want?

19:42.181 --> 19:43.516
Hey, Saeki!

19:43.599 --> 19:45.976
What are you doing
skulking around here?

19:46.060 --> 19:47.520
What about your patrol?

19:47.603 --> 19:49.605
You're supposed to be
on duty today!

19:49.647 --> 19:50.773
SAEKI MATASABURO

19:50.856 --> 19:52.483
Oh, that's right.

19:54.235 --> 19:56.946
Heard he was out again
last night.

19:57.029 --> 19:59.657
You know, what's-his-name.

19:59.740 --> 20:03.327
[laughing]
What was it again? Uzo? Muzo?

20:05.996 --> 20:09.709
Izo! That's it, Izo. Okada Izo.

20:09.792 --> 20:11.419
[♪♪♪]

20:11.502 --> 20:14.380
He was prowling
Tominokoji last night.

20:15.297 --> 20:16.632
Tominokoji?

20:19.260 --> 20:21.637
You can just leave him to me.

20:21.721 --> 20:24.432
If you don't dispose of thugs
like him quickly

20:24.515 --> 20:27.226
a man can't enjoy his sake
in peace.

20:27.309 --> 20:29.562
Are you trying
to pick a fight?

20:29.645 --> 20:32.314
[Saeki]
What's that supposed to mean?

20:32.356 --> 20:34.567
Okada Izo is a manslayer,
you know.

20:37.319 --> 20:40.406
Or was he a "friend" of yours,
Vice-Commander?

20:40.489 --> 20:42.199
In fact, isn't protecting him

20:42.283 --> 20:45.411
the same as picking a fight
with our Aizu patrons?

20:47.413 --> 20:49.790
Saeki's not wrong
about any of this.

20:49.874 --> 20:51.250
This isn't right, Toshi.

20:51.333 --> 20:52.543
[Kondo] Saeki,

20:53.461 --> 20:55.421
I apologize for this trouble.

20:57.006 --> 21:00.384
But Toshi would never do
anything to endanger the corps.

21:00.468 --> 21:01.969
You can rest assured of that.

21:04.054 --> 21:09.310
I need you to give it your all
as a Vice-Commander's Assistant.

21:12.313 --> 21:13.856
Yes, sir. If that's an order
from the Commander,

21:13.939 --> 21:15.149
I can't very well refuse.

21:15.232 --> 21:16.942
Well then,
I'll be off on my patrol.

21:31.248 --> 21:34.877
Boss!
Why is he the same rank as me?

21:34.960 --> 21:35.961
Settle down.

21:37.546 --> 21:40.341
Saeki's attitude is certainly
nothing to be proud of.

21:40.424 --> 21:43.469
But you've noticed it as well,
I'm sure.

21:45.387 --> 21:47.723
His killing intent
is not to be taken lightly.

21:47.807 --> 21:50.351
We'll likely see more men
of his ilk

21:50.434 --> 21:52.186
joining our ranks from now on.

21:52.269 --> 21:55.564
Yeah, we're getting more and
more guys with unknown pasts.

21:55.606 --> 21:59.485
It's getting more and more
difficult to maintain control.

22:02.446 --> 22:04.824
We may need to take
some new measures.

22:11.580 --> 22:13.707
[indistinct chatter, singing]

22:35.479 --> 22:37.314
Looks like the master
of this place

22:37.398 --> 22:39.483
has agreed to our "donation."

22:39.567 --> 22:40.693
Oh.

22:53.289 --> 22:54.582
Come on, have a drink.

22:54.665 --> 22:59.461
Master Serizawa.
You should train us sometime.

22:59.545 --> 23:01.630
It's always booze and women
with you...

23:01.714 --> 23:03.757
our enemies
will walk all over us.

23:07.177 --> 23:10.389
Oume, go ahead and train him.

23:10.472 --> 23:13.392
Me? Are you sure?
Yeah.

23:13.475 --> 23:14.393
[chuckles]

23:14.476 --> 23:15.853
Are you...

23:17.354 --> 23:19.440
really that strong?

23:19.523 --> 23:21.525
You're always
drunk off your ass.

23:22.526 --> 23:24.278
I bet even I could take you.

23:24.361 --> 23:25.988
[Serizawa grumbles]

23:26.071 --> 23:27.448
I may not look it,

23:27.489 --> 23:30.951
but I've cut down
a Hokushin Itto-ryu master, too.

23:31.035 --> 23:32.536
[sighing]

23:32.620 --> 23:34.872
Is that right? Heh.

23:34.955 --> 23:39.168
All right, I like your nerve.
I'll give you a lesson.

23:39.209 --> 23:40.794
Mm.
Huh?

23:42.504 --> 23:45.591
Try and kill me. Right now.

23:45.674 --> 23:46.800
[sniffs]

23:46.842 --> 23:48.052
Hell, if anything

23:49.219 --> 23:51.221
I'll even fight you bare-handed.

23:53.599 --> 23:55.851
I'm the chief commander
of the Mibu Ronin.

23:55.935 --> 23:58.520
If you take me down,
you'll be famous overnight.

23:58.562 --> 24:01.857
The Imperialists
might pay you a fortune.

24:01.941 --> 24:03.817
Or perhaps... Ahem.

24:07.154 --> 24:11.408
Are you afraid of me,
even when I'm unarmed?

24:11.492 --> 24:13.077
[chuckling]

24:19.541 --> 24:20.751
Don't you mock me.

24:25.798 --> 24:26.924
Come on.

24:28.842 --> 24:29.551
[cries out]

24:29.635 --> 24:32.471
[gasping, exclaiming]

24:32.554 --> 24:36.475
Hey, do you all get it now?
This is how I train.

24:36.558 --> 24:39.645
Come try to kill me
whenever you want. Got it?

24:40.980 --> 24:42.106
[women scream]

24:44.650 --> 24:47.486
I'll follow your lead, Serizawa.

24:47.569 --> 24:49.863
Pour it over my hand.

24:53.117 --> 24:56.120
[insects chirring]

24:56.203 --> 24:59.123
[♪♪♪]

25:04.503 --> 25:07.631
[Okada]
You're pretty damn good.

25:07.715 --> 25:10.050
[Hijikata] You've got
some skills yourself.

25:12.428 --> 25:15.597
We'll have another match,
Toshizo.

25:15.681 --> 25:17.224
[Hijikata]
Sure.

25:23.647 --> 25:27.693
[doshin]
You. What are you doing here?

25:34.867 --> 25:36.076
You're...

25:37.786 --> 25:39.288
Okada Izo.

25:39.371 --> 25:40.581
Izo?

25:44.668 --> 25:46.211
Don't come...

25:49.423 --> 25:50.841
You mustn't come.

25:54.553 --> 25:55.846
Don't come.

25:59.224 --> 26:00.851
You mustn't come.

26:05.647 --> 26:06.940
[shudders]

26:12.571 --> 26:14.031
Again...

26:23.415 --> 26:24.875
A man-slayer...

26:26.668 --> 26:28.378
[voice breaking]
A man-slayer like me...

26:29.588 --> 26:30.881
[sniffles]

26:33.425 --> 26:34.760
has no right...

26:38.263 --> 26:39.890
to show up

26:41.058 --> 26:42.184
before Toshizo.

26:43.435 --> 26:45.395
[sobbing]

26:56.990 --> 27:00.119
[man speaking indistinctly]

27:01.578 --> 27:03.664
I guess it was after
you all passed by

27:03.747 --> 27:07.042
he was rummaging through scraps
and other trash to eat.

27:07.084 --> 27:08.585
Eating... garbage?

27:08.669 --> 27:13.632
Yeah.
It was a ghastly sight to see.

27:19.805 --> 27:21.849
It was right here.

27:50.752 --> 27:53.088
Will you let me know
if you see him again?

27:56.800 --> 27:58.886
Before the magistrate's office.

28:01.013 --> 28:02.264
Got it?

28:02.306 --> 28:04.141
Understood.

28:07.811 --> 28:09.271
[man]
It's the man-slayer again!

28:09.313 --> 28:12.983
Move out of my way!

28:17.863 --> 28:19.698
[magistrate]
Hey, go on home now!

28:19.781 --> 28:21.200
[onlooker]
What happened?

28:23.827 --> 28:25.454
[magistrate]
Go home now.

28:27.080 --> 28:28.290
Go home!

28:28.373 --> 28:30.918
[indistinct chatter]

28:37.841 --> 28:39.176
[Kondo]
Toshi.

28:48.852 --> 28:51.021
They both went down
with a single strike.

28:52.814 --> 28:55.275
As far as I know,
there's only one person

28:56.818 --> 28:58.320
capable of a feat
like this...

29:01.156 --> 29:02.282
It's Izo.

29:05.911 --> 29:07.913
I have to find him, and fast.

29:08.956 --> 29:10.999
Do you have any leads?

29:11.041 --> 29:12.501
No.

29:12.542 --> 29:14.169
But he has to be close.

29:16.546 --> 29:18.257
What will you do
when you find him?

29:26.765 --> 29:27.975
Cut him down.

29:32.896 --> 29:34.481
Are you really sure about that?

29:36.984 --> 29:39.695
If you fight Izo
with a heartless blade,

29:39.778 --> 29:41.905
you'll be no different
than a man-slayer.

29:41.989 --> 29:44.700
If I don't do this now,
more people will die.

29:44.783 --> 29:46.493
That won't do for you two.

29:49.788 --> 29:51.123
That won't do!

29:58.005 --> 30:02.009
Did you two meet just to kill?

30:04.136 --> 30:05.262
Remember...

30:07.931 --> 30:10.058
why you aimed
to be the strongest.

30:14.771 --> 30:16.148
You two were...

30:21.153 --> 30:22.237
Friends...

30:24.114 --> 30:24.906
Right?

30:24.990 --> 30:28.118
[♪♪♪]

30:30.954 --> 30:32.456
Before I'm his friend...

30:34.041 --> 30:36.835
I'm the vice-commander
of the Mibu Roshigumi.

30:53.143 --> 30:54.144
Izo...

30:58.315 --> 31:00.400
[bird cawing]

31:26.676 --> 31:28.095
I've been looking for you.

31:29.262 --> 31:30.305
Izo.

31:44.319 --> 31:45.487
Toshizo.

31:50.200 --> 31:51.201
Hey.

31:54.996 --> 31:56.456
It's been a while.

32:02.421 --> 32:03.547
Toshizo.

32:10.387 --> 32:11.430
What is it?

32:16.518 --> 32:17.561
I'm...

32:20.439 --> 32:21.606
I'm...

32:25.110 --> 32:27.737
As I kept cutting people
on command...

32:30.073 --> 32:31.408
And the men I fought

32:33.952 --> 32:35.745
started to look like scarecrows.

32:39.332 --> 32:40.417
Now...

32:42.210 --> 32:44.296
I feel nothing
when I cut them down.

32:50.719 --> 32:52.721
So you've lost your heart?

33:06.860 --> 33:08.278
Honestly...

33:14.743 --> 33:16.620
I didn't want to meet you
like this.

33:18.288 --> 33:19.289
Don't.

33:23.710 --> 33:25.462
Guess we have no choice, Izo.

33:26.505 --> 33:28.131
Don't, Toshizo.

33:31.593 --> 33:34.012
At least I'll be the one
to cut you down...

33:38.642 --> 33:40.435
Vice-Commander, Mibu Roshigumi

33:42.145 --> 33:43.480
Hijikata Toshizo.

33:45.941 --> 33:47.317
Here I come!

33:51.154 --> 33:53.823
[♪♪♪]

33:57.118 --> 34:01.081
I am... Izo the Manslayer!

34:01.164 --> 34:03.291
No, you aren't.

34:10.840 --> 34:12.509
[both grunting]

34:30.150 --> 34:31.860
Damn... you're strong.

34:34.531 --> 34:35.864
Interesting.

34:35.949 --> 34:37.576
[panting]

34:39.034 --> 34:41.079
You're still Izo,
through and through.

34:51.047 --> 34:52.465
From here on,

34:53.882 --> 34:55.802
I'm just... Hijikata Toshizo.

35:01.766 --> 35:04.019
You said it yourself, Izo.

35:04.102 --> 35:05.854
"With wooden swords,
we could fight

35:05.895 --> 35:07.230
as many times as we wanted."

35:07.314 --> 35:09.316
But I guess that's not
an option now.

35:13.361 --> 35:17.741
This is a fight to the death.
Our first and our last duel.

35:24.331 --> 35:28.501
Izo... after this,
we can never do this again.

35:28.585 --> 35:31.421
There's no greater honor
than to fall by your blade.

35:32.339 --> 35:35.592
I know you feel the same. Izo!

35:38.053 --> 35:39.638
[yells fiercely]

35:47.562 --> 35:48.897
[cries out]

35:52.275 --> 35:54.611
Damn, that hurts!

35:54.694 --> 35:57.197
Hey! How's that feel?
Tell me, does a scarecrow bleed?

35:57.280 --> 35:58.740
[both panting]

35:58.823 --> 36:01.826
What you just cut
wasn't a scarecrow, was it?

36:01.910 --> 36:05.497
See? You feel pain, don't you?

36:08.333 --> 36:10.919
And the man I'm fighting
isn't a scarecrow either.

36:11.920 --> 36:15.632
I'm fighting you! Okada Izo!

36:19.260 --> 36:21.513
[both groaning]

36:27.727 --> 36:31.731
Hey... What was it
we were striving for,

36:33.566 --> 36:34.484
Izo?

36:45.995 --> 36:52.293
[♪♪♪]

36:52.377 --> 36:55.505
To become the strongest man
alive, wasn't it?

37:03.179 --> 37:04.723
[exhales sharply]

37:07.058 --> 37:08.351
[sighs]

37:33.501 --> 37:35.879
I don't need something like this

37:38.465 --> 37:40.467
to duel Toshizo...

37:41.718 --> 37:42.969
[sword clatters]

37:45.889 --> 37:47.640
[chuckling softly]

37:53.229 --> 37:54.898
[laughs]

37:56.024 --> 37:57.525
[sword clatters]

38:01.112 --> 38:04.657
That's more like it, Izo.

38:09.788 --> 38:11.289
Alright.

38:15.418 --> 38:16.586
You can continue...

38:18.129 --> 38:19.631
to fight with those.

38:19.714 --> 38:23.051
[♪♪♪]

38:26.763 --> 38:27.764
Boss...

38:40.860 --> 38:42.779
[laughing]

38:51.287 --> 38:52.622
Toshizo,

38:54.707 --> 38:55.834
bring it on!

38:59.754 --> 39:00.880
Yeah!

39:07.262 --> 39:08.888
[exhales fiercely]

39:14.811 --> 39:17.814
[both yell fiercely]

39:20.942 --> 39:24.487
[♪♪♪]

40:06.070 --> 40:07.655
I am Okada Izo!

40:07.697 --> 40:13.411
The strongest man in all Japan!

40:14.704 --> 40:19.167
I'm the greatest samurai
in all of Japan!

40:19.208 --> 40:20.460
[both grunt]

40:23.212 --> 40:25.673
[both panting]

40:30.845 --> 40:33.222
I won!
I won!

40:36.976 --> 40:39.687
[laughing heartily]

40:44.692 --> 40:46.694
Looks like another draw.

40:47.820 --> 40:48.863
Toshizo...

40:52.784 --> 40:54.035
Man...

40:56.579 --> 40:58.831
that was a damn good time.

40:58.915 --> 41:01.209
[laughing]

41:01.250 --> 41:03.169
[groans]

41:12.720 --> 41:19.686
Hey... Toshizo... Someday...

41:21.145 --> 41:22.480
Someday...

41:26.067 --> 41:27.777
we'll do this again.

41:30.655 --> 41:32.740
No matter how much
I boast of my strength,

41:32.782 --> 41:34.742
don't you dare
run away next time.

41:41.749 --> 41:43.001
[sobs]

41:45.920 --> 41:47.088
Huh?

41:47.130 --> 41:49.716
[chuckles]

41:49.799 --> 41:51.843
What's wrong with you,
Toshizo?

41:53.594 --> 41:54.971
You're one to talk.

41:57.724 --> 42:02.186
No matter where you hide,
no matter where you run

42:03.521 --> 42:08.026
I'll find you
and beat the hell out of you.

42:09.694 --> 42:12.155
[chuckles, stammers]

42:15.158 --> 42:16.993
Toshizo...

42:17.076 --> 42:21.122
You're a real weirdo.

42:22.707 --> 42:26.127
We just made
this incredible promise...

42:26.210 --> 42:28.796
So why are you crying?

42:30.048 --> 42:31.674
Shut up!

42:33.301 --> 42:35.636
You're the one who's crying!

42:35.720 --> 42:36.846
Huh?

42:37.930 --> 42:39.015
What?

42:40.349 --> 42:41.768
But why...?

42:41.851 --> 42:46.355
[both laughing and crying]

42:54.113 --> 42:55.573
It's a promise, then.

43:00.912 --> 43:01.913
I promise.

43:07.043 --> 43:09.045
[laughing]

43:18.429 --> 43:20.181
[bell tinkling]

43:20.264 --> 43:23.226
[♪♪♪]

43:26.729 --> 43:30.691
[narrator] After that,
Okada Izo was captured in Kyo

43:30.775 --> 43:32.985
and extradited
to the Tosa Domain.

43:34.612 --> 43:36.739
He was imprisoned
with Takechi Hanpeita

43:36.823 --> 43:40.827
and the rest
of the Tosa Loyalist Party.

43:44.372 --> 43:45.414
[Okada]
Hey...

43:47.583 --> 43:49.127
You...

43:49.210 --> 43:50.628
[guard]
Huh?

43:51.838 --> 43:53.881
A wooden sword...

43:54.882 --> 43:56.884
Can you lend it to me?

44:00.096 --> 44:01.514
A wooden sword?

44:01.597 --> 44:02.640
[scoffs]

44:02.723 --> 44:04.934
What are you gonna do with that?

44:07.436 --> 44:08.938
Toshizo's...

44:10.439 --> 44:11.941
waiting for me.

44:19.448 --> 44:20.992
Toshizo...

44:22.535 --> 44:24.036
is getting stronger...

44:24.954 --> 44:26.122
[chuckles]

44:26.956 --> 44:28.708
...and waiting for me.

44:28.791 --> 44:32.920
[♪♪♪]

44:58.487 --> 45:00.740
Yah!
Tah! Tah!

45:03.618 --> 45:05.453
[chuckles]

45:05.494 --> 45:07.955
[narrator]
Then, on July 3, 1865...

45:08.039 --> 45:14.212
Okada Izo
was executed by beheading.

45:14.295 --> 45:16.964
They say he was swinging
that wooden sword

45:17.048 --> 45:19.175
right up to his final moment.

45:24.347 --> 45:25.473
[grunts fiercely]

45:28.851 --> 45:30.853
I can't believe it.

45:30.937 --> 45:33.314
The man they called
"Izo the Manslayer"...

45:34.857 --> 45:37.568
Once in Edo, and once in Kyo.

45:37.652 --> 45:42.448
To think that's all it took
to forge such a powerful bond.

45:45.076 --> 45:46.994
That's what it means
to cross swords

45:47.036 --> 45:49.330
with your life
on the line.

45:49.372 --> 45:52.917
Social status and personal
beliefs don't matter.

45:54.126 --> 45:58.297
You just throw your pure
strength at one another.

46:00.341 --> 46:04.428
A battle like that
is every samurai's dream.

46:06.555 --> 46:09.725
I'm envious of a bond like that.

46:09.809 --> 46:11.394
It may have been the last dream

46:12.770 --> 46:15.273
either of them ever had.

46:17.400 --> 46:19.068
Their last dream?

46:19.151 --> 46:20.111
Ah...

46:22.196 --> 46:23.489
Sadly...

46:25.032 --> 46:27.785
After that,
the battles we fought...

46:29.704 --> 46:33.082
were a far cry
from any such dream.

46:41.299 --> 46:44.635
Hey, Hijikata,
what are you doing?

46:44.719 --> 46:46.721
The corps regulations.

46:46.804 --> 46:49.265
To keep the riffraff in line.

46:50.099 --> 46:51.475
Eh?

47:01.652 --> 47:02.737
Mm.

47:02.778 --> 47:05.072
How very Toshi. I love it.

47:05.114 --> 47:06.490
You really think so?
Yeah.

47:08.117 --> 47:09.952
We'll fight and clash to keep
the corps' rules in place...

47:10.036 --> 47:11.746
and make sure
everyone stays in line.

47:11.829 --> 47:13.372
"Fight's on!"

47:16.834 --> 47:19.712
Aah!
You didn't have
to tear them, Soji!

47:19.754 --> 47:21.589
I'm impressed you
wrote something so idiotic.

47:21.630 --> 47:23.132
In fact, it's almost brilliant.

47:24.300 --> 47:25.343
Kondo...

47:30.014 --> 47:32.141
Never mind Hijikata's
scribbles

47:32.975 --> 47:34.310
use this one.

47:36.103 --> 47:37.938
Who does he think he is?

47:38.022 --> 47:40.441
Now, now.
Let's see what you've got.

47:45.279 --> 47:46.572
"The Corps Code.

47:49.825 --> 47:53.954
One: Do not stray
from the Way of the samurai.

47:53.996 --> 47:59.085
One: Desertion of the corps
is forbidden.

47:59.126 --> 48:03.047
One: You are forbidden to raise
money without authorization.

48:03.130 --> 48:07.927
One: You are forbidden to
involve yourself in litigation.

48:08.010 --> 48:12.640
One: Do not engage
in personal fights.

48:15.142 --> 48:17.186
Any who violate these articles

48:20.356 --> 48:21.524
must commit seppuku."

48:23.109 --> 48:25.277
That's pretty harsh, isn't it?

48:25.361 --> 48:29.532
Okita. This is no time
for such naive talk.

48:29.615 --> 48:32.743
This isn't Shieikan anymore.

48:32.827 --> 48:35.496
To restore order
to the chaos in Kyo

48:35.538 --> 48:38.916
the unity of our corps
is absolutely essential.

48:38.999 --> 48:41.836
[Okita] But still,
seppuku seems extreme.

48:41.877 --> 48:43.379
Yamanami.

48:44.505 --> 48:45.673
[Yamanami]
What is it?

48:45.756 --> 48:47.299
You're against it, too?

48:48.926 --> 48:50.511
Add two more.

48:58.144 --> 48:59.937
One:

49:00.020 --> 49:01.355
Draw your swords and fight
until you strike down

49:01.439 --> 49:04.233
your opponent
or are struck down yourself.

49:04.316 --> 49:05.443
One:

49:07.027 --> 49:08.654
If you fail to kill
and take a wound to your back

49:08.737 --> 49:09.947
it is seppuku.

49:11.240 --> 49:12.575
[Okita]
That means...

49:13.993 --> 49:15.744
Once you draw your sword,
you must win.

49:15.828 --> 49:17.037
Soji.

49:18.706 --> 49:20.332
This is about resolve.

49:23.794 --> 49:25.504
Without this level of resolve

49:28.090 --> 49:30.301
you can't protect
the things that matter.

49:30.384 --> 49:32.511
[♪♪♪]

49:35.890 --> 49:37.266
I...

49:41.228 --> 49:43.355
don't want to lose
any more comrades.

49:47.568 --> 49:48.652
[Yamanami]
That's true.

49:51.280 --> 49:54.158
The stricter these rules are

49:54.241 --> 49:57.411
the more justification
we'll have to keep

49:57.453 --> 50:00.080
Serizawa's rogue faction
in check.

50:00.122 --> 50:01.415
[Kondo]
A just cause.

50:01.499 --> 50:03.125
[Yamanami]
Yes.

50:03.209 --> 50:05.461
At the very least,
it should slow them down.

50:06.921 --> 50:09.131
[Oume] Is it good?
[Serizawa] Yes.

50:09.215 --> 50:11.133
[Yamazaki]
The Corps Code?

50:13.302 --> 50:17.890
"One: Do not stray
from the Way of the samurai.

50:17.973 --> 50:21.560
One: Desertion of the corps
is forbidden.

50:21.602 --> 50:23.437
One: You are forbidden to raise
money without authorization."

50:23.479 --> 50:25.105
This is Yamazaki.
He can memorize

50:25.189 --> 50:27.691
anything he sees and hears,
down to every detail

50:27.775 --> 50:30.778
and is able to recall it
perfectly.

50:30.861 --> 50:32.488
[Serizawa]
A natural-born spy, huh?

50:32.571 --> 50:35.032
"One: You are forbidden to
involve yourself in litigation.

50:35.115 --> 50:36.867
Anyone who violates
these rules..."

50:36.951 --> 50:38.619
YAMAZAKI SUSUMU

50:38.702 --> 50:40.079
"Seppuku."

50:42.456 --> 50:44.667
[neck cracking]

50:44.750 --> 50:46.502
Mm-- Mm.

50:49.338 --> 50:51.382
The stricter these rules are

50:51.465 --> 50:53.342
the more justification
we'll have

50:53.425 --> 50:57.596
to keep Serizawa's rogue faction
in check.

50:57.680 --> 51:00.391
This is obviously aimed at us.
A just cause?

51:00.474 --> 51:01.767
Those bastards.

51:01.850 --> 51:03.143
We have to do something.

51:03.227 --> 51:05.312
I like it. The "Corps Code."

51:05.354 --> 51:08.357
What?
But this business

51:08.440 --> 51:10.401
about committing seppuku
for breaking them...

51:10.484 --> 51:11.569
I don't like it.

51:11.652 --> 51:13.195
If we play this right,

51:13.279 --> 51:15.990
we could use it
to tighten the noose.

51:16.031 --> 51:17.825
[Serizawa]
Is that so?

51:17.908 --> 51:19.577
[Niimi]
Hey. Good work.

51:19.660 --> 51:22.871
[exclaiming frantically]
Money! Money!

51:29.461 --> 51:30.671
[Serizawa sighs]

51:33.215 --> 51:36.343
[insects chirring]

51:51.317 --> 51:54.486
Half past six. I'll be waiting
at Shinkenji Temple.

52:02.620 --> 52:03.746
Guess who?

52:03.829 --> 52:04.747
[sword slices]

52:04.830 --> 52:06.749
[blood flowing]

52:06.832 --> 52:08.125
[gasps]

52:11.920 --> 52:16.258
[Yoshiaki Dewa's "Chiruran
Shinsengumi Requiem" playing]
